window.docContents[108].resolve({"/Foundations/Coordinates-and-Boundary-Calculus/#PDEAtlas--Foundations--Coordinates-and-Boundary-Calculus--Boundary-Calculus-and-C___-Boundary-Geometry--Scope-of-the-boundary-calculus":{"contents":"The finite compatible chart family assembles into a unique frontier-supported\nmeasure  with the same null sets as intrinsic Hausdorff\nsurface measure. Density-root rescaling identifies the finite-exponent Lᵖ\nspaces of the two measures isometrically, and for finite  the\nintrinsic trace has a norm-preserving atlas-coordinate form.\n\nMathlib supplies the same-dimensional Jacobian change of variables used for\nchart transitions, Hausdorff-measure transport under isometries, and Lipschitz\nnull-set transport. The nonlinear codimension-one area formula, which\nidentifies  with Hausdorff surface measure, is proved in\nthe trace development.\n\n","context":"PDEAtlas\u0009Foundations\u0009Coordinates and Boundary Calculus\u0009Boundary Calculus and C¹ Boundary Geometry","header":"3.3.2.16. Scope of the boundary calculus","id":"/Foundations/Coordinates-and-Boundary-Calculus/#PDEAtlas--Foundations--Coordinates-and-Boundary-Calculus--Boundary-Calculus-and-C___-Boundary-Geometry--Scope-of-the-boundary-calculus"},"/Sobolev-Spaces-and-Weak-Derivatives/Fourier-Sobolev-Spaces/#PDEAtlas--Sobolev-Spaces-and-Weak-Derivatives--Fourier-Sobolev-Spaces":{"contents":"Fractional and negative regularity can be defined through the Fourier\ntransform. On the whole space the\nFourier transform converts differentiation into multiplication by ,\nso one can ask that  be square integrable for\nany real . This gives a Hilbert scale  of tempered\ndistributions.\n\n\n\n","context":"PDEAtlas\u0009Sobolev Spaces and Weak Derivatives","header":"4.5. Fourier Sobolev Spaces","id":"/Sobolev-Spaces-and-Weak-Derivatives/Fourier-Sobolev-Spaces/#PDEAtlas--Sobolev-Spaces-and-Weak-Derivatives--Fourier-Sobolev-Spaces"}});